{
  "name": "Schrödinger harmonic trap",
  "description": "Linear Schrödinger equation in a bowl-shaped potential V = ½ω²r² (ω = 0.1). Left: a packet the exact width of the ground state, pulled to one side, swings back and forth through the centre forever without spreading: a coherent state, the most classical a quantum state gets. Top: a squeezed packet, narrower than the ground state, breathes (spreads and refocuses twice per swing) as it swings. Where they cross they interfere. Period about 3500 steps.",
